From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] vbscript: byte, date, array and dialog built-ins; the Erase statement

A run of VBScript built-ins were E_NOTIMPL stubs or FIXMEs, so scripts
that used them stopped with an error: login and install scripts use
DateDiff, DatePart, Join, Filter, Erase, InputBox and the byte functions
for binary data. ReDim of an array declared "Dim a()" crashed.

- Byte functions: LenB, LeftB, RightB, MidB, InStrB (1 to 4 arguments),
  AscB and ChrB work on the bytes of a string; AscW gives an Integer
  (ChrW(&HFFFF) is -1), and String takes a character code.
- SetLocale and GetLocale keep the script's locale (an LCID or a name;
  SetLocale returns the one before), and conversions use it.
- DateValue and TimeValue keep the date or the time part; DateDiff and
  DatePart count every interval (yyyy, q, m, y, d, w, ww, h, n, s) with
  the first day of the week and the first week of the year.
- Join and Filter (include or exclude, binary or text compare).
- Erase is a statement: a fixed-size array keeps its size with its
  elements emptied; a dynamic array is left with no elements, so UBound
  raises "subscript out of range" until it is ReDim'd; anything else is a
  type mismatch. LBound and UBound take any array and raise error 9 on one
  with no elements.
- VarType of an array is vbArray + vbVariant; TypeName names more types
  ("Variant()", "Byte", "Decimal", ...).
- Escape and Unescape (%XX and %uXXXX); LoadPicture loads a picture file
  (OleLoadPicturePath), and an empty name gives Nothing.
- InputBox shows a prompt with an edit box (title, default text selected,
  position in twips) and returns what was typed, or an empty string on
  Cancel; MsgBox accepts a help file and context.
- Left with a negative length and StrComp with a bad compare mode raise
  "invalid procedure call" as on Windows.

Wine's vbscript tests: run 47714, vbscript 1620, createobj 566 tests, no
failures, as before.

Gate: test/vbsbuiltins-gate.sh (64- and 32-bit cscript in the shell's
desktop; InputBox and MsgBox answered through SendKeys).
Mutants SG_MUTANT_ERASE_NOOP (vbscript/interp.c), SG_MUTANT_LENB_CHARS
(vbscript/global.c).
